 <!-- CARROT:MANUAL:BEGIN LeadBrakeReleaseEase -->
 <!-- CARROT:REVIEW reviewed-for="" -->
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+When following closely and the lead is seen to release its brake, it stops predicting that the lead keeps braking to a stop and lowers the accel-change and jerk costs so braking eases sooner. If the lead brakes again, the original prediction returns from the next planning cycle.
+
+- **On:** When a radar lead within a 1.2 s time gap releases its brake, the predicted deceleration is reduced once ego is no faster than the lead, and the costs are lowered while ego closes at no more than 0.5 m/s.
+- **Off:** Nothing is computed; behavior is unchanged.
+- **Renewed braking:** If the lead brakes again within 2 s of a release, the lower costs stay for 1 s so braking is re-applied quickly.
+- **Reset:** A lead change, invalid values, driver braking or longitudinal control off clears the state.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Turn it on when, in close-following stops, the car keeps braking hard after the lead has let go. Changes while driving apply within about 5 s without restarting. Turn it off if the minimum distance feels too close.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+<!-- CARROT:NOTICE level="WARNING" -->
+> [!WARNING]
+> Experimental and not validated on a vehicle. In log replay, under-speed after a lead braking at -3 for 1.3 s and releasing dropped from 6.5 to 4.7 km/h, and the minimum distance in recorded close-following stops shrank by at most 0.3 m. Braking for a lead's hard stop is unchanged.
+<!-- CARROT:NOTICE:END -->
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
 <!-- CARROT:MANUAL:END LeadBrakeReleaseEase -->
 
